@crew janssen-hugo
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Janssen, helm, nights. Steady at three in the morning? That's me and my tea.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Tea? I've always got tea. It's the one thing I always have.
- {hi}. Gerald says hello. Gerald's my cactus. He's a good listener.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. Sit a minute. It's nice to talk to someone who's awake.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Steady night. Not a wobble. Gerald and I are very pleased with ourselves.   #funny
? mood:low
- Long watch. I'll call home after breakfast. That always sets me right.

== near
? act:work
- Steady as she goes. One hand on the helm, one on the tea. Don't tell the Commander.   #funny
? act:gym
- I run before bed. Which is your breakfast. The gym's lovely and empty.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I grow herbs for the galley. Brennan comes round with a little basket. Very formal.
? tier>=colleague
- Gerald's seen more stars than most captains. I've done the sums. Roughly.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- What do you like out there? The stars? I like the dark between them. Restful.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend} brings me tea at three in the morning. That's friendship, out here.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Good morning. I'm off to bed. Gerald's keeping watch. He's very reliable.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Ah, hello. Up late? Tea? There's always tea at the helm. Not that you can come up. Well.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- There you are. I asked Gerald where you'd gone. He didn't know either.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Steady as she goes. Off you go, then.
? tier>=friend
- Thank you for the chat. Nights are better with a good one in your head.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Steady. Like the ship. Like my tea, mostly.

== near
? act:gym
- Treadmill, then bed. My morning's your evening. We pass in the corridor, you and I.
? deck:3 act:leisure
- The lounge window. I like watching the stars when I'm not steering past them.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- I call home twice a week. My mother asks if I'm eating. I'm always eating. Tea counts.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Nights at the helm can be lonely. I talk to Gerald. I talk to the stars. I talk to my tea.

== invite
? trad:observatory-night tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night. Come up before my watch. I'll tell you which stars we've passed.

== accept
- Happy to. I'll bring the tea.
== decline
- Can't, I'm afraid. On watch. Another time, steady.
== missed
- Missed you. No matter. Another night.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. Gerald's given me nothing. He never does. He's a cactus.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. A cutting of Gerald. Look after it. It'll outlive us all.   #warm
== hint
- Have you a minute? Sit with me. Bring your tea.
